WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.590
- [Reporter] In this
1989 Revlon commercial,

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:05.950
the cosmetics company asked
a question to its customers.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.773
- [Announcer] What makes
a woman unforgettable?

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.530
- A little luck and
the right shade of red.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.940
- [Reporter] The answer to
that question was, of course,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.760
Revlon cosmetics.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.530
For much of the 20th century,

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.860
Revlon products were a
mainstay in the makeup aisle,

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.280
once capturing 1/5 of all
department store cosmetic sales

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.000
in the United States.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.512
But in the 21st century,

00:00:26.512 --> 00:00:30.020
Revlon has found itself
battling declining market share

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.570
and increasingly crowded shelf space.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.403
Now, with the company

00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:36.180
recently averting a bankruptcy filing,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.160
questions remain if the
once unforgettable brand

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.461
is on its way to being forgotten.

00:00:41.461 --> 00:00:44.378
(soft tense music)

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.737
- You know, when you look
wonderful, you feel wonderful.

00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:53.220
And the secret can be the makeup you use.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.180
- [Reporter] Revlon
helped usher in the era

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.910
of color cosmetics in the
first half of the 20th century.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:02.550
The company was founded
in 1932 by Charles Revson

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.010
along with his brother, Joseph,
and chemist Charles Lachman.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.850
It started by selling nail polish

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.150
but quickly moved into lipsticks.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.920
Sales of cosmetics surged
between 1941 and 1946.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.660
Revlon positioned itself
to meet this demand,

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.360
claiming its products were
seen on the fingertips

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.060
and lips of the nation's smartest women.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.580
- Revlon is a brand that,
for decades, really,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.580
for a generation was the
biggest, most ubiquitous,

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.070
sought after, kind of cutting edge brands

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.100
and it was what you thought of

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.670
when you thought of mass market,
yet very desirable makeup.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.530
- [Reporter] The
cornerstones of Revlon's rise

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.330
were mass production and mass marketing.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.300
It spent heavily on advertising,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.100
sponsoring popular TV programs

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.247
and pinning exclusive deals
with beauty shop suppliers.

00:01:51.247 --> 00:01:54.229
- [Announcer] Revlon, the
greatest name in cosmetics,

00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:57.229
presents the 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64,

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.523
yes, "The $64,000 Question."

00:02:04.162 --> 00:02:05.050
- [Reporter] Charles Revson is said

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.573
to have described Revlon's
strategy like this:

00:02:07.573 --> 00:02:09.810
"In the factory, we make cosmetics.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.060
In the store, we sell hope."

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.826
Selling hope helped
bolster the company sales,

00:02:14.826 --> 00:02:18.620
and in the 1960s and
'70s, Revlon branched out,

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.930
expanding into
pharmaceuticals and apparel.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.300
In 1975, Charles Revson died

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.510
and European businessman
Michel Bergerac took the helm.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.300
A year later, Revlon sales
reached nearly $1 billion,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.240
although it was still second
in sales behind Avon products

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.340
with its door-to-door distribution.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.290
The cosmetics conglomerate
kept pace with changing trends

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.072
as more women entered the workforce,

00:02:41.072 --> 00:02:44.644
marketing its products to
on-the-go, career-driven women.

00:02:44.644 --> 00:02:48.203
- [Announcer] Now the world
belongs to Charlie by Revlon.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.939
- [Reporter] But by the early
1980s, sales had flattened,

00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:54.930
and in a decade marked
by hostile takeovers,

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.610
one of the top corporate raiders
had Revlon in his sights.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.640
Businessman Ron Perelman
initiated a hostile takeover

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.900
of Revlon in 1985.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.947
The takeover bid dominated headlines,

00:03:05.947 --> 00:03:09.040
detailing the struggle
between Perelman and Bergerac

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.350
for control of the company.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.180
- He said to me, very proudly,

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:17.650
that he hunted lions and tigers

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.135
so I was not a threat to him.

00:03:20.135 --> 00:03:22.180
- [Reporter] Ultimately,
Perelman prevailed,

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.910
becoming chairman of Revlon's board

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.373
and controlling shareholder.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.560
Perelman enlisted famed fashion
photographer Richard Avedon

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.090
to shoot the unforgettable ad campaign,

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.570
bringing top supermodels
like Christy Turlington

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:37.720
and Cindy Crawford to
be the faces of Revlon.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.404
At first blush, Revlon appeared poised

00:03:39.404 --> 00:03:41.730
to end the century on a high note.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.700
However, its finances were
telling a different story.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.029
Perelman had used junk bonds
to finance the takeover.

00:03:48.029 --> 00:03:51.190
It was assumed he would sell
Revlon's non-beauty businesses

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.800
to pay down this debt.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.790
Instead, he turned his
focus to a failed bid

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.140
to take over Gillette
and this came at a time

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.180
when competition was heating up.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.880
Proctor &amp; Gamble acquired
several makeup brands,

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.260
snatching up 1/3 of the
cosmetics market by 1990,

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.020
compared to Revlon's
share of just over 20%.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.490
At the same time, Revlon
was stretched thin.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.620
It was carrying nine upscale product lines

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.320
with nearly 3,000 individual products.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.539
But women were wearing
less and less makeup

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:21.130
as they moved away from the
bright colors of the '80s

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.260
to more muted, natural looks.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.093
The company launched

00:04:24.093 --> 00:04:27.220
its hit Colorstay
non-transferable lipstick in 1995

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.430
and went public in 1996.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:32.290
However, much of Revlon's pre-tax profits

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:36.160
were going to serve as
its $1.3 billion of debt.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.240
- Late in the century,
it turned into a company

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.860
that was just a little
bit behind the trends.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:41.740
You know, things started,

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.660
fashion started shifting
away from these bright colors

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.683
and Revlon didn't adapt to that change.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:53.060
It caught on somewhat late
to the shift toward skincare

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.960
and skin health and was
still really selling

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.890
kind of these, you know,
these color cosmetics

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.384
that were changing.

00:05:00.384 --> 00:05:02.920
- [Reporter] By 2003,
Revlon had experienced

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.580
16 straight quarters of losses,

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.910
and by 2007, its share of the
cosmetics market had fallen

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.096
to 11% in mass market retailers.

00:05:12.096 --> 00:05:15.490
Despite this, Perelman continued
to keep the company afloat

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.220
with injections of cash in
a revolving door of CEOs

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:22.580
- Mr. Perelman, he said, and
this was more than a decade ago

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.590
in an interview with "The
Wall Street Journal,"

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.630
he said, "For good or bad,
I'm defined by Revlon."

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.560
He led rescues.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.600
He just bailed the company
out over and over again

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.350
as it continued to struggle.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.600
- [Reporter] Revlon tried to
recapture part of the market

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.070
with high profile
acquisitions of Colomer Group

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.740
and Elizabeth Arden.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:44.550
But by 2017, its market share
had dwindled to around 6%.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.390
By then, Revlon was not only
facing stiff competition

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:49.950
from the likes of Proctor
&amp; Gamble and L'Oreal,

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.601
but from startups with serious star power.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.540
Celebrity-backed makeup lines

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.620
like Kylie Jenner's Kylie cosmetics

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.130
had burst onto the scene.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.500
- You know, a company,
whether it's Revlon,

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.110
whether it's CoverGirl,
these are companies

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.760
that have massive
advertising budgets, models,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.750
TV commercials, and with
the rise of social media,

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.850
we're seeing brands that
are driven by influencers,

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:16.190
by Kylie Jenner, who
has a cosmetics company

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:19.230
that has $200 million in annual sales

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.700
even though there's only
less than a dozen people

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:22.980
who work at her company.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.150
And she doesn't spend money on advertising

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.789
because she just has so
many Instagram followers.

00:06:27.789 --> 00:06:30.550
- [Reporter] In 2018,
Perelman provided Revlon

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:33.730
with a financial lifeline and
installed his daughter, Debra,

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:37.170
as CEO, the company's first
female chief executive.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.664
Through much of 2020, widespread closures

00:06:39.664 --> 00:06:42.880
and bankruptcies among
retailers, salons, and spas

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.890
crimped sales of beauty products.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.520
- The main thing is that
our lips are covered

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.560
when we wear masks so lipstick
sales have have fallen off.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:52.900
There used to be a term in the industry

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.383
called the lipstick index and
how much women were spending

00:06:55.383 --> 00:06:58.420
on makeup kind of as a
proxy for the economy,

00:06:58.420 --> 00:06:59.490
and he said, "Well you can't really use

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.950
the lipstick index anymore
because nobody can see our lips."

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.130
- [Reporter] The dip couldn't have come

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.550
at a worst time for Revlon.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:09.850
With a $343 million bond payment looming,

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:13.030
Revlon refinanced its
debt to avoid bankruptcy.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:14.900
- If you look at kind
of some of the analysts

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.370
and some of the industry experts,

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:19.160
they question whether
this deal to save Revlon

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.790
has just kicked the can down the road.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.420
Certainly, old brands,

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.220
brands that are struggling
have revived themselves before.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.800
I would say Revlon has a tougher road

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.438
and it's an entire company, not a brand.

00:07:32.438 --> 00:07:35.120
But it's hard to say where
they're gonna end up.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.340
- [Reporter] Where Revlon ends up

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:39.360
will depend on how it adapts
to the modern beauty landscape

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.420
and if it can inject a little color

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.463
into an otherwise bleak outlook.

